kadam 0.4

The page is called "Paragraphs".
The page background is paper.
The page text is ink.
The page is dark when the system is dark.

A SiteHeader.

Guide section:
    It is full width. It is at most 760px wide. It is centered.
    It has 40px padding on the top and bottom and 24px padding on the left and right.
    It has 14px gap between children.

    A big heading says "Write pages as paragraphs". The text is between 2rem and 2.5rem.
    Muted text, 18px, says "Start a file with kadam 0.4 and describe the page from top to bottom. The order you write things in is the order they appear."

    A heading says "Things and words".
    "A sentence that names a thing makes it. Words that describe it can come in any order, and sentences that start with It describe the thing you just named."
    A code block says "A big heading says \"Meet Lumen.\"\nAfter that, a 50px gap.\nSmall gray text, 18px, says \"Get more for less.\"\nA big black button called download says \"Download\". It has rounded corners."

    A heading says "Sections".
    "A line that ends with a colon holds the indented lines under it. Its words say what it is, or how its lines are laid out."
    A code block says "Hero section, centered:\n    A big heading says \"Plan your week.\"\n\nIn 3 columns:\n    A Feature with the title \"Fast\" and the description \"Seconds.\""

    A heading says "Fill-in-the-blank components".
    "Write components once in components.kdm. Each blank is filled where you use it, and but changes one thing."
    A code block says "A PrimaryButton is a big black button with white text that says ___.\n\nA PrimaryButton says \"Sign up\".\nA PrimaryButton, but blue, says \"Learn more\"."

    A heading says "Fonts".
    "150 free fonts are built in, so naming one is enough. Every other free font is one command away, and your own font files go in the fonts folder."
    A code block says "The page font is Lora.\nThe heading font is Playfair Display.\nText says \"Note\". The font is Caveat."

    A heading says "Effects".
    "Each effect is one sentence, and each one stops for people who prefer reduced motion."
    A code block says "When the cursor moves over it, white pixels pop out around the cursor.\nWhen hovered, a white fill slides in from the left.\nIt appears word by word.\nIt tilts as you scroll."

    A heading says "Fixes, never guesses".
    "When a sentence is not one Kadam knows, the error says why and offers fixes. Run kadam fix to choose one, or kadam fix --first to take the first fix everywhere."
    A code block says "error[KDM2001]: I don't know \"blck\" in: A big blck button says \"Go\"\n = fix 1: A big black button says \"Go\""

    Note:
        It has 16px padding. The background is tint. It has rounded corners.
        "The full list of sentences is in the language spec, section 17, and kadam explain --blocks page.kdm shows what any page is built from."
